{#-
   Identity Provider Configuration for Keycloak
   =============================================
   This file defines external identity providers (IdPs) that Keycloak federates to.

   BOOTSTRAP: applied via --import-realm on first start only, NOT reconciled by
   keycloak-config-cli. It is merged into the aihub-realm.{stage}.json import
   file (see generate_keycloak_realm). Customers configure their identity
   sources here; operator changes made later in the Keycloak admin console
   survive restarts. Updating IdP config on an already-initialized deployment
   therefore requires the admin console (or a fresh realm database) — it does
   not reconcile automatically. The referenced auth flows ("Post Broker Login
   - AIHubAccess Check", reconciled from managed/40) are created in the same
   realm import, so references resolve on first start.

   For Azure Entra ID, configure these environment variables:
   - KEYCLOAK_AZURE_CLIENT_ID: Azure App Registration Client ID
   - KEYCLOAK_AZURE_CLIENT_SECRET: Azure App Registration Client Secret
   - KEYCLOAK_AZURE_TENANT_ID: Azure Tenant ID

   Azure App Registration Setup:
   1. Create App Registration in Azure Portal
   2. Set redirect URI: https://auth.YOUR_DOMAIN/realms/aihub/broker/azure-ad/endpoint
   3. Create client secret and copy value
   4. Grant API permissions: openid, email, profile
   5. Define App Roles in manifest (AIHubAccess, AIHubSysAdmin)
   6. Assign users/groups to roles in Enterprise Applications

   Role Mapping:
   Azure AD App Roles are automatically mapped to Keycloak realm roles. Only these two
   roles have an effect in AI-Hub; the platform reads no other realm roles for authorization:
   - Azure "AIHubAccess" → Keycloak "AIHubAccess" (REQUIRED for login)
   - Azure "AIHubSysAdmin" → Keycloak "AIHubSysAdmin"

   Multi-Tenant IDP-to-Tenant Mapping (Optional, Not Default):
   ============================================================
   The platform supports automatic tenant assignment based on which identity
   provider a user authenticates through. This is useful when each Azure AD
   app registration represents a different tenant/organization.

   To set this up:
   1. Create a tenant group under /tenants/ in Keycloak (e.g., /tenants/tenant-a)
   2. Create a corresponding tenant in the AI-Hub application
   3. Add a separate identity provider (e.g., "azure-ad") with the
      customer's Azure AD app registration credentials
   4. Add a "Hardcoded Group" IDP mapper on that identity provider:
      {
        "name": "tenant-mapper-tenant-a",
        "identityProviderAlias": "azure-ad",
        "identityProviderMapper": "oidc-hardcoded-group-idp-mapper",
        "config": {
          "syncMode": "INHERIT",
          "group": "/tenants/tenant-a"
        }
      }
   5. Users authenticating via that IDP will be automatically assigned to
      the tenant group. Group membership is additive — logging in via
      multiple IDPs accumulates tenant memberships.

   Note: ${CLAIM.preferred_username} in the username-mapper is a Keycloak
   IdP mapper template, not an environment variable — it must stay literal.
-#}
{
  "realm": "aihub",
  "identityProviders": [
    {
      "alias": "azure-ad",
      "displayName": "Microsoft Entra ID",
      "providerId": "oidc",
      "enabled": true,
      "trustEmail": true,
      "storeToken": false,
      "linkOnly": false,
      "firstBrokerLoginFlowAlias": "first broker login",
      "postBrokerLoginFlowAlias": "Post Broker Login - AIHubAccess Check",
      "config": {
        "clientId": "$(env:KEYCLOAK_AZURE_CLIENT_ID)",
        "clientSecret": "$(env:KEYCLOAK_AZURE_CLIENT_SECRET)",
        "tokenUrl": "https://login.microsoftonline.com/$(env:KEYCLOAK_AZURE_TENANT_ID)/oauth2/v2.0/token",
        "authorizationUrl": "https://login.microsoftonline.com/$(env:KEYCLOAK_AZURE_TENANT_ID)/oauth2/v2.0/authorize",
        "logoutUrl": "https://login.microsoftonline.com/$(env:KEYCLOAK_AZURE_TENANT_ID)/oauth2/v2.0/logout",
        "userInfoUrl": "https://graph.microsoft.com/oidc/userinfo",
        "issuer": "https://login.microsoftonline.com/$(env:KEYCLOAK_AZURE_TENANT_ID)/v2.0",
        "jwksUrl": "https://login.microsoftonline.com/$(env:KEYCLOAK_AZURE_TENANT_ID)/discovery/v2.0/keys",
        "defaultScope": "openid email profile",
        "validateSignature": "true",
        "useJwksUrl": "true",
        "pkceEnabled": "true",
        "pkceMethod": "S256",
        "syncMode": "FORCE",
        "clientAuthMethod": "client_secret_post",
        "hideOnLoginPage": "false",
        "backchannelSupported": "false",
        "icon": "pi-microsoft"
      }
    }
  ],
  "identityProviderMappers": [
    {
      "name": "email-mapper",
      "identityProviderAlias": "azure-ad",
      "identityProviderMapper": "oidc-user-attribute-idp-mapper",
      "config": {
